The first sketch put one displaced unit neatly beside the screen. I made that displacement playable. A visitor chooses a tile, then the open cell; the tile enters and its old position becomes the new vacancy. The repeated field keeps its rule as the opening travels. The warm selection color marks a temporary action, while the screen itself stays teal on the warm paper ground.

